        "verse": 12
      },
      "raw_locator": [
        {
          "book": "HEB",
          "chapter": 11,
          "verse": 12
        }
      ],
      "en": "Therefore as many as the stars of the sky in multitude, and as innumerable as the sand which is by the sea shore, were fathered by one man, and him as good as dead.",
      "ko": "이러므로 죽은 자와 방불한 한 사람으로 말미암아 하늘에 허다한 별과 또 해변의 무수한 모래와 같이 많이 생육하였느니라",
      "source_text_hash": "ee43c236b7897637190c95038048be9a5fda32b63d53a7c2857411e8a7dbb187",
      "translation_text_hash": "f95813ebd70b8bb53e9d32c3cad66502802a7b308fb3354f5c5e3e504360b120",
      "translation_policy": "krv-1961-source-mapped",
      "source_edition": "KRV-1961",
      "mapping_type": "normal",
      "mapping_note": null,
      "raw_texts": [
